00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:55.540
But I feel like forget about it generating like where you are on the map and trying to visually represent that.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:18:11.020
There is just an issue with like there's no real sense of the course other than going back into the menu and checking out the top down view to see the entire layout, you know, from a top down angle and being like, oh, yeah, that's where the green is.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:12.640
Like, let me adjust my guy.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:17.740
Like, it's not clear from the actual like action screen that you're presented.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:29.100
Yeah, you kind of do like you would get the feel for how how accurate, not so much accurate, but how sensitive these things are.

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.120
If you played this game a lot, I'd imagine.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:40.440
But as it stands now, you do have to do calculus, basically, to figure out how this relates to how it ends up on the screen.

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:45.900
And I will stand up a little bit for like the actual visual visual representation.

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:56.400
Like it it it's probably the most realistic view we've seen, but it doesn't so much that doesn't so much mean that it's useful or fun.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.340
So, yeah, you do.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:11.640
You would have to go back to that menu just like, oh, yeah, OK, now I can kind of make a connection between what this map in this whole look like and what I'm seeing through my digital eyes here.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:14.900
But, yeah, I agree.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:25.180
And then I mentioned the power meter, which is interesting because it's not the balance of that power meter is not equal at all.

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:41.580
And that's something that, you know, might be apparent, but really requires the manual to fully grasp that basically there are it looks it looks almost like the map for 10 yard fight, you know, where you have like the different yard lines and everything.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:45.780
And then the two touchdowns on the north and south of it.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:47.640
Those are red bars.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:51.860
And basically there are three clicks you need to do on your power meter.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.760
The first click starts your swing.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:58.440
And then as it goes up, it is indicating your power.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:09.440
However, the power goes from like 0%, 1%, 2%, 3%, 7%, 22%, 44%, 50%, 88%.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:16.720
It's like the 50% mark is a red line that is not in the middle of said power meter.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:23.060
The 50% mark is closer to the top than like maybe it's like 75% of the way to the top.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:29.520
So, OK, the 50% is the 75%, but then the 100% isn't the full bar.

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:31.880
The 100% is the end of the green.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:41.460
You can actually go above 100% into the red zone, the top of the bar, but then that's going to cause you to overswing.

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:49.840
And it will, no matter how perfectly you swing, it will, you know, curve your ball a little bit because you overswung,

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:57.300
which is, I understand, a mechanic in golf to just swing harder and face the consequences in exchange for gaining more yards.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:04.340
However, a really interesting setback is that in every other golf game we played on the NES for the power meter,

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:09.000
even to get to the very top, you have to be precise.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:13.860
If you want to hit 100 and, I don't know, 175% like this game lets you,

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:18.100
you'd have to click the A button again at the very top.

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:20.000
And this game does not do that.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.560
You only get one chance.

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:29.220
And if you don't press the A button at all, you automatically lock in to 175% of your swing

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.920
with no chance to, like, come back down and swing again.

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:40.560
It just locks into what is the next A press, the one that controls, well, how straight on did you hit the ball?

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:46.020
And that you want to hit as close to where it started at 0% to line up a shot.

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:51.820
And again, that could be something that is very confusing to a first-time video game golfer.

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:56.220
We have played enough golf games that I think that concept is readily apparent to us.

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:58.060
But I wouldn't say that that is obvious.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:02.100
They should probably put a golf ball, like, next to, you know,

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:07.400
like a visual representation of a golf ball next to the 0% to, like, lock in the idea of, like,

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:10.240
oh, yeah, and then this is where I hit the golf ball.

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:15.060
All in all, three presses, really just two that matter.

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:18.940
But technically, if you're just starting off on the beginning of the course

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:22.140
and you just want to hit the ball really hard, there's only one press that matters,

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:24.440
and that's how close you get to 0%.

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:33.320
Okay, so as far as the power meter goes and, like, how weirdly it's marked and, I don't know.

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:34.920
I have some defense for it.

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:38.820
Not saying, again, that it's well communicated,

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:46.580
but one would say if they're going for verisimilitude,

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:51.520
I think, like, so it looks like it's going on, like, a logarithmic scale or something,

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:52.980
and that sort of makes sense.

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:57.200
Like, when you're going for a really low-power thing,

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:00.640
you kind of feel like you have a bit more control over it.

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:06.820
Like, if you're trying to putt two feet compared to if you're trying to putt, like, five feet,

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:13.020
you might be able to eyeball that and, like, muscle memory that with your swing.

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:17.020
But if you're trying to really hammer something,

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:21.480
but you're trying to, you know, shave however many yards off

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:25.820
or add however many yards, like, that's going to be really hard to dial in.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:27.380
And I think that kind of makes sense.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:37.060
Like, if you are really whacking something like you would be at the top of this power meter,

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:41.860
the variation is going to be much more wild.

00:23:42.580 --> 00:23:45.720
And so I think that that feels a bit more realistic

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:49.580
than something that's just going on, like, a linear scale from zero to 100,

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:54.060
even if there is some sort of, like, really crush it button.

00:23:55.060 --> 00:24:01.980
And then I think that the accuracy or, like, I guess the hook or pull is pretty intuitive.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:04.900
Like, if you hit too early, then you're going to move in one direction.

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:06.920
If you hit too late, you're going to move in another.

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:10.860
Again, like, it could have been communicated more clearly,

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:16.760
and I think the other aspects of this game that seem hard,

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:18.740
like, that are kind of encumbering,

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:21.700
like the amount of time it takes to redraw

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:23.540
and the fact that in the distance,

00:24:23.540 --> 00:24:27.180
it's hard to really tell where your ball is

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:31.360
until the game is sort of updating your entire screen.

00:24:31.580 --> 00:24:35.480
Like, that doesn't help with giving you, like, live feedback.

00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:41.500
So I don't think that the power meter is crazy bad.

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:44.180
It's weird that there's a red line for 50%,

00:24:44.180 --> 00:24:45.440
and it's a weird spot,

00:24:45.680 --> 00:24:50.700
because I didn't know that that was the 50% mark until much later.

00:24:51.100 --> 00:24:54.260
But it's not the worst design thing in the world.

00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:59.460
I mean, I don't think in a vacuum it's the worst thing in the world.

00:24:59.460 --> 00:25:05.200
I do think that because it's used for every part of this game,

00:25:05.200 --> 00:25:06.460
it doesn't change.

00:25:06.980 --> 00:25:08.600
That's what bothers me the most.

00:25:08.780 --> 00:25:09.880
Where, like, I don't know,

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:12.620
I need something different when I'm putting,

00:25:12.860 --> 00:25:14.720
and I'm three, and, you know, whatever.

00:25:14.900 --> 00:25:16.680
I'm two feet away from the hole.

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:20.940
But, like, the visual meter didn't change at all.

00:25:21.100 --> 00:25:24.380
Just, like, what it represents changes.

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:27.580
So, like, sometimes at the, you know,

00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:30.520
at my first stroke,

00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:34.000
I'm hitting the same spot on the power meter

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:36.820
as I am for, like, my putt when I'm, like, five feet away,

00:25:36.860 --> 00:25:39.080
because now it's, like, recalculated

00:25:39.500 --> 00:25:41.100
how much power this means, you know?

00:25:41.200 --> 00:25:43.440
And, like, again, looking back at NES golf,

00:25:43.780 --> 00:25:45.040
the putt meter looks different,

00:25:45.060 --> 00:25:46.660
and I can sort of contextualize it.

00:25:46.760 --> 00:25:48.340
It's smaller, and I realize, like,

00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:50.140
okay, it's smaller,

00:25:50.140 --> 00:25:52.420
I need to go with a smaller amount,

00:25:52.480 --> 00:25:54.300
like, of the percentage of this bar.

00:25:54.600 --> 00:25:55.680
But this is just, like,

00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:58.780
I guess I feel like I'm just supposed to guess now.

00:25:59.040 --> 00:26:02.820
I agree. Putting is a completely different game, really.

00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:05.260
I feel like even between that,

00:26:05.320 --> 00:26:06.940
like, even when I'm, like, halfway to the hole,

00:26:07.420 --> 00:26:09.840
like, still going to 50 or going to 100%

00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:13.600
is, like, not going to give me the same result

00:26:13.600 --> 00:26:14.660
as it did on my first putt,

00:26:14.700 --> 00:26:16.600
like, depending on how close I am to the hole.

00:26:17.460 --> 00:26:18.640
And, you know, of course,

00:26:18.660 --> 00:26:20.700
in other golf games, that's true, too.

00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:21.800
If you're using, like,

00:26:22.860 --> 00:26:24.640
if you're using a different club or whatever,

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:25.780
like, it'll have different meters,

00:26:25.840 --> 00:26:27.280
but it's represented to me.

00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:29.420
This is just, like, okay, yeah, do it again.

00:26:29.420 --> 00:26:33.040
We've recalculated what everything on this meter means,

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:34.500
and it's invisible to you.

00:26:34.700 --> 00:26:35.860
So, like, I'm still, like,

00:26:35.920 --> 00:26:37.600
kind of confused when that comes up.

00:26:37.740 --> 00:26:39.860
I will just add that, Sean,

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:40.880
I do agree with you

00:26:41.540 --> 00:26:42.980
that I do think some of these

00:26:42.980 --> 00:26:45.260
are actually interesting changes

00:26:45.260 --> 00:26:47.100
to the way that, you know,

00:26:47.140 --> 00:26:48.020
the power meter specifically,

00:26:48.160 --> 00:26:49.760
interesting changes to the way

00:26:49.760 --> 00:26:51.200
you can play golf on the NES.

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:52.380
And I'm not necessarily saying

00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:53.540
that they're bad.

00:26:53.540 --> 00:26:54.900
I'm saying it's just,

00:26:56.120 --> 00:26:57.620
you know, I was just highlighting

00:26:57.620 --> 00:26:59.040
how different it is

00:26:59.040 --> 00:27:01.660
from the other NES golf games we've played

00:27:01.660 --> 00:27:03.320
and just kind of how,

00:27:04.020 --> 00:27:06.460
you know, to talk to Joe's point a little bit,

00:27:06.880 --> 00:27:10.160
how extreme hitting something softly

00:27:11.120 --> 00:27:14.140
might be compared to hitting something really hard.

00:27:14.300 --> 00:27:15.600
Like, I think it's really easy

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:20.280
to have a great first stroke in any course.

00:27:20.280 --> 00:27:22.060
Like, it's really easy to hit the ball hard.

00:27:22.180 --> 00:27:25.920
But it's really hard to perfect, like, that,

00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:30.800
you know, 30 feet away and so on section of the game

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:32.700
because it is kind of hard to tell.

00:27:32.880 --> 00:27:36.580
And yeah, I guess it does help to know percentage points.

00:27:36.580 --> 00:27:38.520
And the manual does lay them out for you.

00:27:38.620 --> 00:27:39.940
It does help to know, like,

00:27:40.200 --> 00:27:44.060
what's 50% versus what's 100% versus what's 10%

00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:47.320
because they do also tell you,

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:49.620
specifically if you're on beginner mode,

00:27:49.760 --> 00:27:51.080
but technically if you're on expert mode,

00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:52.780
there's an easy way to find out in the manual.

00:27:53.060 --> 00:27:55.680
They do tell you how hard...

00:27:55.680 --> 00:27:56.860
100% is.

00:27:57.120 --> 00:27:59.000
Yeah. Each thing can hit 100%.

00:27:59.000 --> 00:27:59.880
So theoretically,

00:28:00.020 --> 00:28:02.300
if you're stuck in the sand,

00:28:02.300 --> 00:28:05.000
but you're only 40 feet away,

00:28:05.300 --> 00:28:07.740
you could do the math on the,

00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:08.760
you know,

00:28:08.860 --> 00:28:12.020
the sand wedge at 100% hits for the men.

00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:13.500
It hits 80 yards.

00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:15.460
So if I'm 40 feet away,

00:28:15.720 --> 00:28:18.120
I want to hit this thing at 50%,

00:28:18.120 --> 00:28:19.340
give or take the wind,

00:28:19.960 --> 00:28:21.660
to, you know, to get within the realm.

00:28:21.920 --> 00:28:24.480
It's just, it goes back to what you're saying about

00:28:24.480 --> 00:28:27.260
sometimes it does feel like you're doing more math

00:28:27.260 --> 00:28:29.300
than you're doing sports.

00:28:29.620 --> 00:28:32.600
You know? Like in baseball games,

00:28:32.780 --> 00:28:35.320
I never have to think about the kind of things

00:28:35.320 --> 00:28:37.160
that real life baseball players,

00:28:37.380 --> 00:28:38.580
you know, like the heads up stuff

00:28:38.580 --> 00:28:40.760
that real life baseball players have to do.

00:28:40.900 --> 00:28:42.400
And so I'm not sure why I have to do that

00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:43.720
in this golf game.

00:28:43.860 --> 00:28:45.580
Like why it can't be a little,

00:28:45.760 --> 00:28:46.880
you know, a little more laid back

00:28:46.880 --> 00:28:49.600
and a little more intuitive to the player.

00:28:50.200 --> 00:28:51.920
Intuitive is the operative word there,

00:28:51.920 --> 00:28:56.920
I think, because I think golf as like in its essence,

00:28:57.160 --> 00:28:58.700
like the very core of golf

00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:00.440
is making calculations

00:29:00.440 --> 00:29:02.320
of how you should hit this thing

00:29:02.320 --> 00:29:05.800
because that's really all you're doing.

00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:08.660
Like there's no, there's no twitch reflex.

00:29:08.920 --> 00:29:10.600
There's, it's all about

00:29:11.400 --> 00:29:12.920
what's going through your head

00:29:12.920 --> 00:29:14.620
before you swing

00:29:14.620 --> 00:29:16.560
and then executing that.

00:29:16.800 --> 00:29:19.220
So I think that you're always going to have

00:29:19.220 --> 00:29:20.880
this sort of, this,

00:29:21.040 --> 00:29:23.300
you know, napkin math

00:29:23.300 --> 00:29:25.160
be a part of these games.

00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:27.760
It's just, how do you make that feel

00:29:27.760 --> 00:29:28.920
more breezy

00:29:30.380 --> 00:29:31.700
for the, for the player?

00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:34.460
I mean, that's exactly what I was going to say too,

00:29:34.580 --> 00:29:37.740
where it's like, the intuitive is a good word for it

00:29:37.740 --> 00:29:39.060
because like, I don't golf,

00:29:39.260 --> 00:29:40.960
but I got to imagine that like,

00:29:41.300 --> 00:29:42.560
even like the best golfer

00:29:42.560 --> 00:29:44.680
is not doing numerical math

00:29:44.680 --> 00:29:47.480
in their head. They're doing intuition math.

00:29:47.600 --> 00:29:48.660
They're doing visual things.

00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:50.220
They're saying, okay, if I, I feel that,

00:29:50.380 --> 00:29:51.820
if I feel like if I hit it this hard,

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:53.440
it'll go this far. And again,

00:29:53.680 --> 00:29:54.840
bringing it back to NES golf,

00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:56.200
like, that's what that felt like to me.

00:29:56.320 --> 00:29:57.920
I was never like, okay,

00:29:58.100 --> 00:29:59.960
what's the, how many yards do I need to hit it?

00:30:00.100 --> 00:30:01.180
Okay. 15 yards.

00:30:01.180 --> 00:30:02.820
And I, and at this percentage,

00:30:02.880 --> 00:30:03.820
that'll be about this.

00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:05.000
I'm just like looking at it.

00:30:05.080 --> 00:30:06.660
I'm like, okay, it's, it's about that distance

00:30:06.660 --> 00:30:07.660
and the arrows pointing this way

00:30:07.660 --> 00:30:08.500
and the wind's going that way.

00:30:08.560 --> 00:30:10.160
So I bet I got to go about to here

00:30:10.160 --> 00:30:11.280
on the meter roughly,

00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:14.320
you know, I'm like, it felt more realistic to like

00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:15.940
how I would be thinking in golf.

00:30:16.380 --> 00:30:17.780
On the other hand though,

00:30:17.940 --> 00:30:18.880
I feel like this,

00:30:19.420 --> 00:30:20.700
like with the percentage points

00:30:20.700 --> 00:30:21.780
being all over the place

00:30:21.780 --> 00:30:22.620
on the power meter,

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:26.100
I think that makes it almost easier.

00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:28.080
Like if you're not really focused

00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:29.760
on being as precise as possible,

00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:31.720
I think that the,

00:30:31.720 --> 00:30:33.560
the way that they have it set up

00:30:33.560 --> 00:30:35.600
makes it easier to kind of just sort of

00:30:36.220 --> 00:30:38.140
go with what feels right.

00:30:38.640 --> 00:30:39.620
I guess what,

00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:41.700
what made me have like the problem with that

00:30:41.700 --> 00:30:43.980
is, is the part a couple of times.

00:30:44.200 --> 00:30:45.780
Well, yeah, the putting, but like a couple of times,

00:30:45.820 --> 00:30:47.040
like I, I,

00:30:47.300 --> 00:30:48.820
I take my first drive

00:30:48.820 --> 00:30:51.020
and I, I go straight to the,

00:30:51.020 --> 00:30:52.260
the red line or whatever.

00:30:52.260 --> 00:30:53.780
And like, it gets me so far or whatever.

00:30:54.040 --> 00:30:56.040
Then I'm putting and I go straight to the red line

00:30:56.040 --> 00:30:57.580
and, and it's a good putt.

00:30:57.640 --> 00:30:59.480
And I'm like, okay, did I have to do,

00:30:59.720 --> 00:31:01.540
why didn't I have to adjust

00:31:01.540 --> 00:31:03.280
anything I was doing to putt?

00:31:03.400 --> 00:31:04.720
Like if I could close my eyes

00:31:04.720 --> 00:31:06.600
or, you know, block out the other side of the screen

00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:07.700
and just look at the,

00:31:07.700 --> 00:31:09.480
the meter and do the same thing

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:10.720
and have a great putt

00:31:10.720 --> 00:31:11.860
and have a great drive,

00:31:12.100 --> 00:31:13.020
just depending on like

00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:14.000
how far away I am. And like,

00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:17.280
I feel like I'm not, I'm not changing like what I'm doing

00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:18.160
to make it feel like, okay,

00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:19.500
now I'm putting. Okay,

00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:20.540
now I'm chipping,

00:31:20.840 --> 00:31:21.820
whatever that even means.

00:31:21.820 --> 00:31:24.140
But like, you know, that's what bothered me about it.

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:26.320
It was, it never felt like I, I was the one making decisions.

00:31:26.320 --> 00:31:28.260
Like, okay, we've changed it now to putting mode.

